0..75 Comment "// The Rust extern `f(x: Option<&u32>, n: u32) -> u32` as a function row of"
76..138 Comment "// the foreign boundary, admitted against its witness records."
139..141 Comment "//"
142..214 Comment "// A function type means a Hoare triple over its arguments\' and result\'s"
215..293 Comment "// realisers. `Option<&u32>` is realised by the null niche, so `f`\'s triple is"
294..367 Comment "// `deref_or`\'s at `u32`. Each argument\'s and the result\'s witness record"
368..440 Comment "// summarises its realisers, read off its code by Rust\'s default layout."
441..443 Comment "//"
444..519 Comment "// `admit(declared, row)` compares rustc\'s printed layouts with the records"
520..599 Comment "// clause by clause, answering `Admitted` or `Unrealised` with the first clause"
600..672 Comment "// that fails. Each extern below differs from the row in one clause. The"
673..746 Comment "// checker holds the layout program\'s integer comparisons as neutrals, so"
747..774 Comment "// admission is a run here."
775..777 Comment "//"
778..859 Comment "// - see: `ledger/diagnostics/BoundaryUnrealised.Niche.gandr` — an extern block"
860..940 Comment "//   refused at check time by the clause it fails, `BoundaryUnrealised.<clause>`"
941..1019 Comment "// - see: `pathological/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the predicate"
1020..1071 Comment "//   chosen through the layout, refused `Undecided`"
1072..1146 Comment "// - see: `model/specification/niche-realizability.gandr` — `deref_or`\'s"
1147..1194 Comment "//   triple and the tagged layout\'s equivalence"
1195..1273 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/boundary.gandr` — the row, the witness record and"
1274..1286 Comment "//   `admit`"
1287..1353 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/layout.gandr` — Rust\'s default layout"
1354..1432 Comment "// - see: Wagner, Eisbach and Ahmed, _Realistic Realizability: Specifying ABIs"
1433..1508 Comment "//   You Can Count On_, OOPSLA 2024, doi:10.1145/3689755, § 3.1 and § 4.2"
1510..1584 Comment "// The Rust side, built by rustc 1.98.0-nightly (f28ac764c 2026-06-23) for"
1585..1656 Comment "// x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Its layouts are from `rustc --edition 2024"
1657..1725 Comment "// --crate-type=lib -Zprint-type-sizes` over the eight externs, with"
1726..1782 Comment "// `size_of`, `align_of` and `needs_drop` for each type:"
1783..1785 Comment "//"
1786..1813 Comment "//     #[unsafe(no_mangle)]"
1814..1874 Comment "//     pub extern \"C\" fn f(x: Option<&u32>, n: u32) -> u32 {"
1875..1922 Comment "//         match x { Some(r) => *r, None => n }"
1923..1931 Comment "//     }"
1932..1934 Comment "//"
1935..2002 Comment "//     type              size  alignment  discriminant   needs drop"
2003..2062 Comment "//     Option<&u32>      8     8          none (niche)   no"
2063..2122 Comment "//     u32               4     4          -              no"
2123..2182 Comment "//     u64               8     8          -              no"
2183..2242 Comment "//     &u32              8     8          -              no"
2243..2302 Comment "//     Tagged            16    8          -              no"
2303..2363 Comment "//     Option<Box<u32>>  8     8          none (niche)   yes"
2364..2423 Comment "//     Packed            4     1          -              no"
2424..2426 Comment "//"
2427..2505 Comment "// `Tagged` is `#[repr(C)] struct Tagged { tag: usize, ptr: *const u32 }`, the"
2506..2569 Comment "// tagged layout of `Option<&u32>` written out, and `Packed` is"
2570..2646 Comment "// `#[repr(C, packed)] struct Packed { v: u32 }`. The externs other than `f`"
2647..2719 Comment "// each differ from the row in one clause: `g` takes `n: u64`, `a` takes"
2720..2789 Comment "// `n: Packed`, `h` takes `x: &u32`, `t` takes `x: Tagged`, `b` takes"
2790..2858 Comment "// `x: Option<Box<u32>>`, `w` answers a `u64`, and `k` takes no `n`."
2860..2869 Comment "// `Nat`."
